":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm rejecting PKT-0011 again, for the same reason as the last review. The test file is fine; the packet's executor log still doesn't record the surprising behaviours the tests pin, which the contract requires.\n\n**Scope and budget:** the diff changes one file, the new `tests/unit/formatchecker.tests.js` (563 lines). That is within the target and within budget (at most 2 files and 800 diff lines). No production code changed and no existing tests changed.\n\n**Test quality:** this is a proper characterization of what the code does today, not a rewrite of it.\n- **Extension ↔ format:** a full round trip over every canonical extension, plus a check that the table has no duplicate ids. It also covers aliases, `pdfa`→`pdf` going one way only, ids that only map from format to extension, case-insensitivity, a leading dot or space not being stripped, a `TypeError` on a non-string value, and `undefined`/`null`/empty input.\n- **Classification:** a table over the five format checks, including edge rows (OFORM_PDF counted as OOX, PDFA as a browser-editor format, the canvas and TeamLab ids, unknown).\n- **Signature detection:** in-memory magic-byte buffers for each image type, truncated buffers one byte short of each signature, the 1000-byte limit on the SVG search, and the logged-and-swallowed error path for `null`. It also pins that `%PDF` and ZIP input are not detected and that only xlsx is detected inside a ZIP, with tests on both sides of the 8KB search window. Finally, `getOfficeZipFormatBySignature(null)` throws while its sibling function guards against `null`.\n- **`getAllFormats`:** shape and category order, malformed entries, caching per file path, retry after a read failure, invalid JSON, JSON that isn't an array, and the rejection when there is no context. Every temporary directory is cleaned up.\n\nThe assertions are precise (`toBe`/`toEqual`, logger call counts), and I found no weak or wrong ones.\n\n**What still blocks approval:** the contract says \"surprising behavior is recorded in the packet, not fixed\", and the \"Executor log\" section still has only the factory's attempt and block entries. These surprises from the tests are not recorded:\n- ZIP detection recognises xlsx only, and only in the last 8KB.\n- `getOfficeZipFormatBySignature(null)` throws a `TypeError`.\n- PDF is not detected from its `%PDF` header.\n- `pdfa` is written back as `pdf`.\n- Calling `getAllFormats('')` without a context throws a `TypeError`.\n\nThe earlier attempts failed because the factory flagged edits to the packet file as out of scope. The release note says Theseus 0.7.2/0.7.3 fixed that, so the executor can add the log now.\n\nVERDICT: REJECT Record the surprising behaviours in the packet's Executor log (xlsx-only ZIP detection in the last 8KB, the TypeError on null in getOfficeZipFormatBySignature, no %PDF detection, pdfa written back as pdf, getAllFormats('') without a context throwing a TypeError); the test file is acceptable as is.","ttft_ms":2397,"type":"result","duration_ms":19069,"uuid":"21d6cf47-67e8-4507-b40e-870179b1c4bd","ttft_stream_ms":907,"time_to_request_ms":368,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":203,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":23,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":2,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":33,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":7,"request_build":13},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":73,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":214,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":228,"process_anon_mib_result":138,"process_peak_rss_mib":257,"process_cpu_ms_turn"